{"author":{"id":"1e0a6ff3e01313072cf7b3803c158c22d01a37717237fe198e814e781752b172"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1785300623,"nonce":"XtVAp/W8Js8Tg3QKjv/nGxuBMco=","title":"b4 review tui: reply buffer built from applied commit drops --- notes","message":"Reported by Matthieu Baerts:\nhttps://lore.kernel.org/tools/bc88076e-2629-45bf-ab20-242f823dde4e@kernel.org\n\nWhen a patch carries a note under the three-dash line, the note is\ndropped when the patch is applied during review (expected), but that\nalso means the note is gone when replying to the patch from the review\nTUI — the maintainer cannot see or respond to the author's below-the-cut\nremarks.\n\nReporter suggests building the Reply view from the original lore email\ninstead of the applied commit.","files":null}]}